      "writtenOn": "2017-01-26T23:07:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Isn\u0027t it more appropriate here to call nvmem_lock_cache()? The task which did the write() should be the one to commit, no? Additionally, nvmem_save() would know if something hasn\u0027t changed. That way, we\u0027re not assuming implementation details of the nvmem_mutex() outside of the lock and unlock functions (ignoring us setting write_in_progress);",
      "revId": "94a5f82c78f9bf65262025e68de721a60af32371",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aa59a84b_3a2270e7",
