        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-01-27T03:11:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "there could be no writes without locking the mutex, if someone calls commit in this case there definitely nothing to write.\n\nBut come to think of it, the check should be different: if there is no lock (task id \u003d\u003d TASK_ID_COUNT) - nothing to do.\n\nIf the current task matches - proceed to commit.\n\nIf a different task calls this - return an error.",
      "revId": "94a5f82c78f9bf65262025e68de721a60af32371",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
